            {
                "entry_id": "ae1e193a-e9e7-30b6-a4bc-03c73ede14aa",
                "word": "thane",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "21ec51cb-2672-4f99-9e0f-331af0999384",
                        "entry_id": "ae1e193a-e9e7-30b6-a4bc-03c73ede14aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "thanes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "81fb10ed-6e03-376b-a23f-888cdcb33ef5",
                        "entry_id": "ae1e193a-e9e7-30b6-a4bc-03c73ede14aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A rank of nobility in pre-Norman England, roughly equivalent to baron."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c0691b8-e2f2-4237-8172-1c579c19d6ae",
                                "sense_id": "81fb10ed-6e03-376b-a23f-888cdcb33ef5",
                                "text": "The Anglo-Saxon thanes were in all respects the predecessors of the Norman barons.\nThe title of thane seems to have supplanted that of gesith, which appears only in the earner Anglo-Saxon laws, a denomination that may originally have designated the attendants or companions of the king, and whose wergild being triple that of the simple freeman, were, therefore, denominated not only gesithcund men, but six-hynde men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4ba6bd1-abff-40ed-b691-d2f06fd50a23",
                                "sense_id": "81fb10ed-6e03-376b-a23f-888cdcb33ef5",
                                "text": "The little island of Iona became the refuge of the sons and some thanes of Athelfrith, banished by Edwin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89313c97-c966-4e22-b644-f8f73cb4ca81",
                                "sense_id": "81fb10ed-6e03-376b-a23f-888cdcb33ef5",
                                "text": "Never need you fear\nfor a single thane of your sept or nation,\nyoung warriors or old."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16681a05-7a43-427a-8421-4b8ac6801f6b",
                                "sense_id": "81fb10ed-6e03-376b-a23f-888cdcb33ef5",
                                "text": "2000, Wulfstan, Robert Boenig (editor and translator), Sermo Lupi ad Anglos, Anglo-Saxon Spirituality: Selected Writings, page 144,\nAlthough some serfs escape from their lord and turn away from Christendom to the Vikings and after this it happens that the clash of swords becomes common to thane and serf, if the serf utterly kills the thane, he lies unpaid by all of the serf's kin."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a0a8342-ee38-4284-a3cc-6d423605febe",
                        "source_entry_id": "ae1e193a-e9e7-30b6-a4bc-03c73ede14aa",
                        "source_sense_id": "81fb10ed-6e03-376b-a23f-888cdcb33ef5",
                        "source_sense_description": "A rank of nobility in pre-Norman England, roughly equivalent to baron",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lehnsmann",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lehnsmann",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e15c7fd0-ea1e-39eb-b5b5-8e100c271b06",
                                        "entry_id": "7f3e0c78-8800-37f8-8d11-f84e4ea17435",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Empfänger eines Lehens vom Lehnsherren"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a80fa2b-6bdd-4f09-9fb9-090cffa6a1d1",
                                                "sense_id": "e15c7fd0-ea1e-39eb-b5b5-8e100c271b06",
                                                "text": "„Da die Dienste des Lehnsmannes insbesondere Kriegsdienste umfassten, wurde das Lehnswesen in der fränkischen Monarchie jahrhundertelang die Grundlage der Heerverfassung und der sozialen Organisation des Heiligen Römischen Reichs.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "73f91c41-fc4c-4f5e-8360-6ebf42332675",
                        "source_entry_id": "ae1e193a-e9e7-30b6-a4bc-03c73ede14aa",
